.TH BIGFLOATSHIFTLEFT 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatShiftLeft, bigFloatShiftRight \- shift a dynamic float mantissa
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigFloatShiftLeft(BigFloat *x, int64_t bits);
int bigFloatShiftRight(BigFloat *x, int64_t bits);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shifts use int64_t counts, modify a temporary mantissa, then normalize and
round toward zero at the current precision. Negative counts reverse direction.
Right shifts discard low mantissa bits and can produce zero; these are not
merely exponent changes. Left shifts grow scratch before normalization.
A zero count does nothing.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation failure, INT_MAX for size/exponent range failure,
or -2 for invalid precision. Errors leave the input unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
